<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43620" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sĕnātōrĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		senator, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			senator</i>, <i>senatorial</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cujus aetas a senatorio gradu longe abesset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Imp. Pomp. 21, 61</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ordo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 1, 23</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 18,
			43</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sall. C. 17, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. J. 62,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">104,
			1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dignitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					12, 1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subsellia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Corn. 1, p. 449</span></i>
			 Orell.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consilium,</span>”
				<i>the deliberations of the Senate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 1, 2, § 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">munera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 1, 1, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 35</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litterae,</span>”
				<i>speeches made in the Senate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 2, 1, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">album,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 42 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aetas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					14, 8, 1</span></i>
			 et saep.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid tam civile, tam senatorium, quam illud,
					etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Pan. 2, 7</span></i>
			. —<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sĕnātōrĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a
			senator</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homines nobiles cum paucis senatoriis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. Rep. Ord. 2, 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			 p. 277 Gerl.</div>
